   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Water flows into and out of a tank. Let A(t) be the amount of water in the tank, in gallons, at time t hours, for \\( t \\ge 0 \\). The rate of change of A is \\( R(t) = 7 - 6 t \\) gallons per hour. At time t = 3, there are 45 gallons. Find the value of \\( A(5) \\), in gallons, and show the setup for the calculation.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 11,
      "units": "gallons"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The known value and the accumulated change combine as \\( A(5) = A(3) + \\int_{3}^{5} \\left(7 - 6 t\\right)\\,dt \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99033",
         "rule_named": "net change theorem"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "An antiderivative of the rate is \\( - 3 t^{2} + 7 t \\), so the integral is \\( \\left[- 3 t^{2} + 7 t\\right]_{3}^{5} = -34 \\).",
         "mathjson": -34,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99003",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "So \\( A(5) = 45 + \\left(-34\\right) = 11 \\) gallons.",
         "mathjson": 11,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "combine with the known value"
      }
   ],
